settings.liquid:
{%- comment -%}
  Claude Code, 2026-08-27 - the hero banner CSS, moved here from the standalone
  `hero_banner_css` custom-html section that used to sit between this section and
  `research_standard`.

  Why it moved: `section-spacing-collapsing` emits
  `#shopify-section-<id> + * { --previous-section-background-hash: <hash> }`, so an
  injected section becomes the 'previous section' for whatever follows it. Its hash
  (0, no background) matched research_standard's own, and the theme collapsed that
  section's 80px top padding to nothing - 'Our Evidence Standard' sat flush against
  the banner. Every other page keeps its 80px because nothing sits in that gap.

  Scoping also changed: the old rules used the section CLASS, and this page has TWO
  image-with-text-overlay sections, so they were landing on the `transparency` band
  too. `{{ section.id }}` resolves at render time and keeps them here.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
@media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > picture > img,
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > img { object-position: right center; }

  /* This section wraps its text in .prose inside a positioning div - NOT in
     .v-stack the way collection-banner does. Targeting .v-stack here matched
     nothing and the description ran on under the flask. */
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > div { max-width: clamp(320px, 46vw, 660px); }
}

@media screen and (max-width: 699px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media::before {
    background-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(10, 14, 22, 0.85) 0%, rgba(10, 14, 22, 0.62) 22%, rgba(10, 14, 22, 0.00) 58%);
  }
}

/* The theme wraps a liquid block in a plain <div>, which takes a gap in the
   text stack and pushes the vertically-centred heading up. The style inside
   still applies when its wrapper is display:none - CSS is not affected by it. */
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .prose > div:has(> style) { display: none; }
</style>
